  "worked_solution": "We are told that there were $40$ disposable cups in total. The tape diagram for those shows $5$ boxes. Therefore, each box in the diagram above represents $40÷5=8$ disposable cups.   \n\nNow, we fill the number $8$ in each box of both tapes:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/multivariable/14187307/assets/b3ed4d72509ba29446f6da8919d81b4cce2dc57d6b80c8496f832c2ec5e95616.png)\n\nSince there are $6$ boxes corresponding to lemonade servings, and each box represents $8$ servings, the number of servings was:\n\n$$\n6\\times 8=48\n$$\n\nSo, Timmy had $48$ lemonade servings in total.",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
